PixVid is a breakthrough for high-res, real-time video generation. Instead of working in compressed latent space, it "lifts" a pretrained video diffusion model to directly draw every frame in pixel space—no VAE bottleneck, no retraining from scratch.

With just 1.3M clips (~4K GPU-hours), PixVid matches or beats its latent baseline: VBench 84.8 vs 84.1, and handles 2× resolution (960 × 1664) with the same token grid per frame. Depth-based editing stays perfectly in sync even during fast motion (98% vs 83% retention), and action latency drops from 495 ms to 34 ms—while streaming at 29 fps.

It’s a recipe for sharper, larger, and instantly controllable AI-generated video, ready for interactive rendering, robotics, AR, and more—all by swapping out the VAE for a smarter, pixel-level head.

